<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mubariz al-Din Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1363">1363</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mubariz al-Din Muhammad was the founder of the Muzaffarid dynasty in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. A servant of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>, he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazd">Yazd</a> from its atabegs in 1319 and, after the Ilkhanate broke up, seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerman">Kerman</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> in 1353 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a> from the Injuids. Known for his harsh piety, he was deposed and blinded by his sons in 1358.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mubariz-al-din-muhammad.jpg" alt="Mubariz al-Din Muhammad" width="320" height="331" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 16th century artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Attack_of_the_sons_of_Mubariz_al-Din_on_their_father,_folio_from_a_manuscript_of_Nigaristan,_Iran,_probably_Shiraz,_dated_1573-74_(assassination_detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
